+		<!-- advc: New game speed modifiers ...
+			 Set to 100 in the DLL by default. -->
+		<!-- advc.130r: start -->
+		<!-- Affects the per-turn chance of incrementing or decrementing AI diplo
+			 memory counters. (Some count up, e.g. "years of peace", others decay,
+			 namely remembered diplo actions such as "you declared war on us".)
+			 Percentages above 100 make it less(!) likely for counters to be
+			 changed, i.e. make diplomacy more inert.
+			 During the early game, counters that count up receive
+			 special treatment: they get adjusted to game length and the
+			 MemoryRand adjustment only takes effect gradually. -->
+		<element type="iAIMemoryRandPercent" minOccurs="0"/>
+		<!-- Affects the per-turn chance of AI civs reaching out to other
+			 human or AI civs with offers, requests or demands. The contact
+			 probability is 1/ContactRand, i.e. a percentage above 100
+			 makes the AI less likely to reach out.
+			 Peace offers and requests for joining a war are exempt from
+			 this adjustment. -->
+		<element type="iAIContactRandPercent" minOccurs="0"/>
+		<!-- Adjusts the minimum delay in between any two consecutive
+			 AI-to-human offers, requests and demands of the same type.
+			 A higher percentage means a longer pause, ergo less frequent
+			 AI-to-human contact. -->
+		<element type="iAIContactDelayPercent" minOccurs="0"/>
+		<!-- advc.130r: end -->
+		<!-- advc.130k: Adjusts the duration of sustained peace that is needed
